---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';

const seoMetaData = {
  description: 'Sveltos binary license: the published images of sveltos-agent, drift-detection-manager, sveltos-applier, mcp-server and techsupport are free to use; features that need a license key require a Sveltos Enterprise license.',
  slug: 'license/',
  // Reachable only by the link: search engines must not index it
  noindex: true
};

const restrictions = [
  'access, request or attempt to obtain the source code of the Software;',
  'modify the Software or create derivative works from it;',
  'reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the Software, except to the extent that applicable law expressly permits this despite this restriction;',
  'remove, bypass, disable or circumvent any license key check or other technical protection in the Software, or enable a Licensed Feature without a valid license.',
];
---

<Layout title="License: Sveltos" seo={seoMetaData}>
  <header>
    <Hero
      variant="standard"
      headline="Sveltos Binary License"
      subhead="Install and use Sveltos freely, in production, on any number of clusters. No registration, no key. Premium features need a separate license."
      isWhiteBg={true}
      isSmall={true}
    />
  </header>

  <main>
    <Section sectionStyles="py-[3rem] px-[1.5rem] xl:px-[3.5rem] bg-white">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto w-full flex flex-col gap-12">

        <div class="bg-primary/5 border border-primary/10 rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-3xl mb-4">In short</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray leading-relaxed mb-0">
            Most of Sveltos is open source under the Apache License 2.0. This license covers only the five components whose source code is not published:
            sveltos-agent, drift-detection-manager, sveltos-applier, mcp-server and techsupport.
            All other Sveltos components are open source and are released under the Apache License 2.0, not under this license.
            You can run their published images and executables, including commercially, on any number of clusters, and redistribute them unmodified, including as part of your own product.
            Features that are enabled by a license key (for example pull-mode, ClusterPromotion, grouping, restricted RBACs, etc.) require a Sveltos Enterprise license.
            Without a license key those features do not work fully, so you can run the images without a license and without worrying: whatever works is free to use.
            This summary is for convenience only: the terms below are the license.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-3xl mb-4">Common questions</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray leading-relaxed mb-4">A summary for convenience only: the terms below are the license.</p>
          <dl class="space-y-4 text-lg text-gray leading-relaxed">
            <div>
              <dt class="font-semibold">Can I install Sveltos freely?</dt>
              <dd>Yes. No registration and no license key.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="font-semibold">Can I use it in production?</dt>
              <dd>Yes.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="font-semibold">Can I include it in my product and sell it?</dt>
              <dd>Yes.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="font-semibold">What if I do nothing?</dt>
              <dd>Nothing to worry about. You can run Sveltos without a license key, and whatever works without a key is free to use. Premium features need a key to work fully.</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="font-semibold">What if I need a premium feature?</dt>
              <dd>
                That needs a separate license from Sveltos.
                See <a href="https://website.projectsveltos.io/pricing/" class="text-primary font-semibold">https://website.projectsveltos.io/pricing/</a>.
              </dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>

        <div>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray leading-relaxed mb-4">Copyright (c) 2026 Sveltos SRL. All rights reserved.</p>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray leading-relaxed mb-0">
            This license applies to the container images and executable files published by Sveltos SRL ("Sveltos") for the following Sveltos components:
            sveltos-agent, drift-detection-manager, sveltos-applier, mcp-server and techsupport (the "Software").
            It does not apply to the other Sveltos components, which are open source and are released under the Apache License 2.0.
            It does not grant any right in the source code of the Software, which is proprietary and confidential.
            By pulling, installing or running the Software you agree to the terms below.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-3xl mb-4">1. Grant of use</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray leading-relaxed mb-0">
            Sveltos grants you a worldwide, non-exclusive, non-transferable, royalty-free license to install and run the unmodified Software,
            for any purpose including production and commercial use, on any number of clusters and nodes.
            No registration, fee or license key is required. Licensed Features are covered by Section 2.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-3xl mb-4">2. Free Features and Licensed Features</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray leading-relaxed mb-4">
            "Licensed Features" are the features of the Software that are enabled only by a valid license key issued by Sveltos.
            They include, as described in the Sveltos documentation at
            <a href="https://projectsveltos.io" class="text-primary font-semibold">https://projectsveltos.io</a>
            and as updated by Sveltos from time to time, pull-mode, ClusterPromotion, grouping of multiple clusters behind a single agent instance and restricted RBACs.
            All other features are "Free Features".
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Licensed Features need a license key. Without one, the Software does not provide them, or provides them only in a limited way.
            You can therefore run the Software without a license key and without worrying about licensing:
            whatever it does without a key is a Free Feature and is free to use under this license,
            as long as you do not bypass or circumvent the license key check (Section 4).
          </p>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray leading-relaxed mb-0">
            Using a Licensed Feature in any environment requires a valid, current license issued by Sveltos, under a separate written agreement.
            This license does not grant any right to use Licensed Features.
            To get a license, see <a href="https://website.projectsveltos.io/pricing/" class="text-primary font-semibold">https://website.projectsveltos.io/pricing/</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-3xl mb-4">3. Redistribution</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray leading-relaxed mb-0">
            You may copy and redistribute the unmodified Software, for example by mirroring the container image into a private or air-gapped registry,
            or by including it in your own product or service, which you may charge for, provided that you keep this license file and all notices unchanged.
            Each recipient receives the Software under this license directly from Sveltos, and Licensed Features still require a valid license under Section 2.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-3xl mb-4">4. Restrictions</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray leading-relaxed mb-4">You may not, and may not allow others to:</p>
          <ol class="list-[lower-alpha] pl-6 space-y-2 text-lg text-gray">
            {restrictions.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
          </ol>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-3xl mb-4">5. Ownership</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray leading-relaxed mb-0">
            Sveltos and its licensors keep all rights, title and interest in the Software. No right is granted except as expressly stated in this license.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-3xl mb-4">6. Termination</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray leading-relaxed mb-0">
            This license ends automatically if you breach any of its terms. On termination you must stop using the Software and delete all copies.
            Sveltos may also end this license for the Software, or for a specific version of it, by giving written notice.
            Sections 4, 5, 6, 7 and 8 survive termination.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-3xl mb-4">7. Disclaimer of warranty and limit of liability</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray leading-relaxed mb-0">
            THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
